  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let w be a multilinear commutator word, and assume that G is a group where\nthe set of w-values is covered by finitely many cyclic subgroups. Is it true that the\nverbal subgroup w(G) is finite-by-cyclic?\n   This is true for lower central words (G. Cutolo, C. Nicotera, J. Algebra, 324, no. 7\n(2010), 1616–1624).                                                          M. Morigi",
